{"ratings":[{"id":"F1","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Slow daemon responses can cause tests to run without a slot, creating CPU contention with active gate suites under load."},{"id":"F2","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"After a heartbeat outage and delayed recovery response, the running suite loses its replacement slot and another suite can start alongside it."},{"id":"F3","consequence":"test","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Running the related test files together in one process produces a false test failure, while the factory's process-isolated suite is unaffected."}]}